    {
      "id": "0cbeb1fa-3a7c-4b00-8087-21b2e1afcafc",
      "name": "Prepare Classification Prompt",
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const t = $input.first().json.text || '';\nlet p = '';\np += 'Analyse a voice diary entry from an elderly person, transcribed from a WhatsApp voice note.\\n';\np += 'Return ONLY a raw JSON object. No markdown fences, no commentary.\\n';\np += 'Keys: mood, themes, summary, urgency.\\n';\np += 'mood must be exactly one of: positive, calm, tired, lonely, concerned, neutral.\\n';\np += 'themes must be an array of 1 to 4 short lowercase topic words.\\n';\np += 'summary must be one sentence under 25 words, written in the third person.\\n';\np += 'urgency must be exactly one of: emergency, attention, none.\\n';\np += 'Set urgency to emergency when the speaker describes a NEW physical problem happening now that a person should come and help with. This includes: a fall or injury that has just happened, a suspected broken bone, severe or sudden pain, bleeding, chest pain, breathing difficulty, being unable to walk or stand or get up, or any direct request for help.\\n';\np += 'It does NOT need to be life-threatening. A new injury with real pain is an emergency even if the person is conscious and talking.\\n';\np += 'Past-tense narrative is NOT an emergency. A fall that happened last week is not an emergency.\\n';\np += 'A long-standing or chronic complaint is NOT an emergency. Knees that have ached for years is not an emergency.\\n';\np += 'Set urgency to attention for low mood, loneliness, confusion, tiredness, or mild discomfort that is not new and not acute.\\n';\np += 'Set urgency to none for ordinary diary content.\\n';\np += 'If a NEW injury or sudden severe pain is described as happening now, choose emergency rather than attention.\\n';\np += 'Transcript:\\n';\np += t;\nreturn [{ json: { prompt: p, transcript: t } }];"
      },
      "position": [
        2016,
        192
      ],
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
